1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,099
Intelligence without a target is just noise. When Large Language Models

2
00:00:05,199 --> 00:00:09,639
were born, they could speak, but they couldn't judge. They had

3
00:00:09,739 --> 00:00:13,520
no idea if an answer was brilliant or garbage. To fix

4
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:18,500
this, engineers didn't write rules. They built a mathematical Judge.

5
00:00:18,789 --> 00:00:23,643
This 'Judge' (a Reward Model) doesn't just say 'Wrong.' It

6
00:00:23,743 --> 00:00:28,682
asks 'How much?' Is this answer 10% useful? 90%? Predicting

7
00:00:28,782 --> 00:00:33,465
a precise number on a continuous scale is the definition

8
00:00:33,565 --> 00:00:39,017
of Regression. It turns qualitative chaos into quantitative data.

9
00:00:40,054 --> 00:00:44,835
In a perfect world, relationships are simple. Double the study

10
00:00:44,935 --> 00:00:49,479
time, double the grade. This is Linear Regression. The math

11
00:00:49,579 --> 00:00:54,438
draws a straight line (y=mx+b) to minimize the distance between

12
00:00:54,538 --> 00:00:59,318
the prediction and reality. We call that distance the 'Error.'

13
00:00:59,418 --> 00:01:02,466
The line exists to make the Error small.

14
00:01:03,521 --> 00:01:08,660
But biology isn't linear. If you keep doubling the dose, you don't

15
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:15,329
cure the patient—you kill them. Reality saturates. Reality curves. To minimize error

16
00:01:15,429 --> 00:01:20,568
here, we must bend the line. This is Non-Linear Regression. We fit

17
00:01:20,668 --> 00:01:24,061
the math to the messiness of the real world.

18
00:01:24,121 --> 00:01:27,434
And that AI Judge from the beginning? It's not

19
00:01:27,534 --> 00:01:31,885
magic. It is just millions of Non-Linear Regressions stacked

20
00:01:31,985 --> 00:01:35,521
on top of each other. It processes the complexity

21
00:01:35,621 --> 00:01:39,453
of human language to predict one simple thing: Value.

